From b0a52b666c02bb3888406c1ced4a0b9f1ced Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Galih Tama <galpt@v.recipes>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 11:30:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] STD: hook select_task_rq Fair/Idle-only

Hook select_task_rq via std_select_cpu. Keeps Fair/Idle-only
routing above deadline with no new class. Respects affinity and
small-system guard; pinned, migrating, core (rq-wide, may
over-skip) and EXT pass through, stop never intercepted, DL/RT
pass through (SIS, no counters, LLC tier removed). Steers Fair/Idle
with SMT-aware idle selection denying cross-group only when
in-group allowed exists. Placement stays at wakeup time; the pick
path is untouched so the disabled cost is near-zero.

Signed-off-by: Galih Tama <galpt@v.recipes>
---
 kernel/sched/core.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/kernel/sched/core.c b/kernel/sched/core.c
index 1754d9f95..e5dba0588 100644
--- a/kernel/sched/core.c
+++ b/kernel/sched/core.c
@@ -3634,6 +3634,15 @@ int select_task_rq(struct task_struct *p, int cpu, int *wake_flags)
 
 	if (p->nr_cpus_allowed > 1 && !is_migration_disabled(p)) {
 		cpu = p->sched_class->select_task_rq(p, cpu, *wake_flags);
+		/*
+		 * STD Fair/Idle-only routing shim above deadline: SMT-aware
+		 * idle selection for housekeeping, denying cross-group only
+		 * when in-group allowed exists; honoring affinity; stop never
+		 * intercepted, pinned/migrating/core(rq-wide, may
+		 * over-skip)/EXT pass through; DL/RT pass through (SIS, no
+		 * counters); LLC tier removed. Wakeup only; pick untouched.
+		 */
+		cpu = std_select_cpu(p, cpu);
 		*wake_flags |= WF_RQ_SELECTED;
 	} else {
 		cpu = cpumask_any(p->cpus_ptr);
-- 
